              body: "<ul><li><b>Infective Endocarditis Stigmata:</b><br>1. <i>Osler Nodes:</i> Painful, tender, raised nodules on finger/toe pads (Immune complex deposition).<br>2. <i>Janeway Lesions:</i> Painless, erythematous macules on palms and soles (Microemboli).<br>3. <i>Roth Spots:</i> Exudative, edematous hemorrhagic lesions of the retina with pale centers.</li><li><b>Koplik Spots:</b> Tiny white/blue spots on an erythematous base on the buccal mucosa opposite the molars. <i>Pathognomonic for:</i> Measles (appears before the rash).</li><li><b>Virchow's Node:</b> Enlarged, hard, non-tender left supraclavicular lymph node. <i>Signifies:</i> Metastatic abdominal malignancy (Gastric Cancer, known as Troisier's sign).</li><li><b>Sister Mary Joseph Nodule:</b> Palpable nodule bulging into the umbilicus. <i>Signifies:</i> Advanced intra-abdominal malignancy (Gastric/Ovarian).</li></ul>" 
